{
  "id": "ye1imu3",
  "title": "CHAPTER 12: ANIMAL KINGDOM",
  "order": 12,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "9o1n7iv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction to Animal Kingdom"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Animals are multicellular, heterotrophic eukaryotes displaying cellular, tissue, organ, or organ-system level organization.",
        "Body symmetry transitions from asymmetrical (Porifera) to radial (Cnidaria, Ctenophora) and bilateral (Platyhelminthes to Chordates).",
        "Coelom classification divides animals into acoelomates, pseudocoelomates (Nematoda), and eucoelomates (Annelida to Chordata).",
        "Phylum Arthropoda represents the largest group in Animalia, distinguished by jointed appendages and chitinous exoskeletons.",
        "Chordates are defined by the presence of a notochord, dorsal hollow nerve cord, and pharyngeal gill slits at some developmental stage."
      ],
      "id": "qrq4vi4"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Major Phyla",
          "value": "11 Primary Phyla",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Largest Phylum",
          "value": "Arthropoda",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Symmetry Types",
          "value": "Radial & Bilateral",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Germ Layers",
          "value": "Diplo / Triploblastic",
          "icon": "info"
        }
      ],
      "id": "a474mao"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6n880ex",
      "content": "Kingdom Animalia consists of multicellular, eukaryotic, heterotrophic organisms. They lack cell wall, show locomotion at some stage of life, and exhibit complex organ systems. Animals are classified mainly on the basis of level of organization, symmetry, germ layers, coelom, segmentation and presence of notochord."
    },
    {
      "id": "fqogj8t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Levels of Organization"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5v4twi7",
      "content": "• Cellular level – Porifera"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7iqwnd9",
      "content": "• Tissue level – Cnidaria"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q7dypga",
      "content": "• Organ level – Platyhelminthes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b3ipqo8",
      "content": "• Organ system level – From Nematoda onwards"
    },
    {
