    },
    {
      "id": "c3pfuji",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Non-Chordates Overview"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gpupa72",
      "content": "Non-chordates lack notochord and dorsal nerve cord. Major phyla include Porifera, Cnidaria, Platyhelminthes, Nematoda, Annelida and Arthropoda."
    },
    {
      "id": "n0itdlj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Phylum Porifera"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9d5zyq7",
      "content": "Aquatic animals with pores (ostia) and canal system. Cellular level organization. Skeleton made of spicules or spongin."
    },
    {
      "id": "c5jyxgj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Phylum Cnidaria (Coelenterata)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hzgevzb",
      "content": "Diploblastic, radially symmetrical animals with tentacles and stinging cells (nematocysts). Exhibit polymorphism."
    },
    {
      "id": "j386vjf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Phylum Platyhelminthes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vx7h1tr",
      "content": "Flatworms, triploblastic, acoelomate. Mostly parasitic. Example: Taenia."
    },
    {
      "id": "ssjsop5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Phylum Nematoda"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aikjuhc",
      "content": "Roundworms, pseudocoelomate, complete digestive system. Example: Ascaris."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 12: ANIMAL KINGDOM",
      "id": "4rhqg08"
    },
    {
      "id": "5pu3t9w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Phylum Annelida"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wv1s7fh",
      "content": "Segmented worms with true coelom and closed circulatory system. Example: Earthworm."
    },
    {
      "id": "9by561m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Phylum Arthropoda"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "twdra07",
      "content": "Largest phylum. Segmented body, jointed appendages, chitinous exoskeleton, open circulatory system."
    },
    {
