    {
      "id": "0cf5haz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. Phylum Chordata"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4tzd1jo",
      "content": "Chordates possess notochord, dorsal hollow nerve cord, pharyngeal gill slits and post-anal tail at some stage."
    },
    {
      "id": "3vcnxvo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12. Vertebrate Classification"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3v8x63f",
      "content": "Vertebrates are divided into Pisces, Amphibia, Reptilia, Aves and Mammalia."
    },
    {
      "id": "ikxli2k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "13. Pisces, Amphibia & Reptilia"
