    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rnkycat",
      "content": "Pisces: Aquatic, gills, 2-chambered heart.<br></br>Amphibia: Land &amp; water, 3-chambered heart.<br></br>Reptilia: Dry scales, mostly 3-chambered heart (except crocodile)."
    },
    {
      "id": "lasxfdr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "14. Class Aves"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6h9x30i",
      "content": "Warm-blooded, feathers present, 4-chambered heart, pneumatic bones."
    },
    {
      "id": "mpwze2i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "15. Class Mammalia"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "06frisi",
      "content": "Warm-blooded animals with mammary glands, hair, diaphragm and 4-chambered heart. Most are viviparous."
    },
